	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Thonk 'Thonkiconn' 3.5 mm switching jack socket, PCB vertical. Checked against doc/Thonkiconn_Jack_Datasheet-new.jpg, which Thonk publishes under model no. PJ398SM - the same part this footprint is named PJ301M for. Three terminals in a line on the barrel axis; measured from that axis the datasheet gives -4.92 / +3.38 / +6.48 and this footprint uses -5.0 / +3.5 / +6.5, so it is the datasheet rounded, worst case 0.12 mm out. Terminal slots are specified 0.5-0.6 x 1.3-1.5; this uses plain o1.1 round holes, the usual synth-DIY simplification, proven by assembled Doubleplus_Pulses boards. Pads are named not numbered - S = datasheet 1, TN = 2, T = 3.")
